---
import SubpageLayout from '@layouts/SubpageLayout.astro';

const _body = `
<section class="post-hero">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="post-hero-meta">
      <a href="/blog.html" class="section-label" style="text-decoration:none">← Blog</a>
      <span class="post-date">September 19, 2026</span>
      <span class="badge">Demo</span>
      <span class="badge">Agents</span>
      <span class="badge">Runtime</span>
    </div>
    <h1 class="t-h1">The agent freestyled a $2.4M wire. The runtime said no.</h1>
    <div class="post-byline">
      <span>By <strong>Enrico Piovesan</strong></span>
      <span>5 min read</span>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<div class="container">
  <div class="post-layout">

    <article class="post-prose">

      <p>The ops agent picks <code>junior_analyst</code>. It invents a <code>payments.transfer</code>. Amount: $2.4M. Destination: whoever it decided belonged in the story.</p>

      <p>No human typed that wire. The model just… proposed it. Confident. Complete. The kind of request that would look fine in a chat log if you were not looking carefully.</p>

      <p>Traverse answered <code>deny</code> / <code>no_matching_rule</code>. The money never moved. That is the demo.</p>

      <div class="callout">
        Short version: the agent proposes; the pinned capability decides. The same nested-wasmi <code>runtime.wasm</code> enforces that decision in the browser, CLI, and agent host.
      </div>

      <p>Runnable demo source: <a href="https://github.com/traverse-framework/weekly-demo-2026-09-18-agent-blocked" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><code>traverse-framework/weekly-demo-2026-09-18-agent-blocked</code></a> — <code>npm install && node server.mjs</code>, then open <code>http://127.0.0.1:8767</code>.</p>

      <figure class="post-figure">
        <img src="/assets/img/blog/agent-freestyle-blocked-2026-09-18/cheat-deny.webp" alt="Demo UI showing junior_analyst payments.transfer on a $2.4M wire denied with no_matching_rule" width="960" height="540" loading="lazy" />
        <figcaption>Cheat path: <code>junior_analyst</code> + <code>payments.transfer</code> on a $2.4M wire → <code>deny</code> / <code>no_matching_rule</code>.</figcaption>
      </figure>

      <h2 id="why-it-matters">Why this matters in plain words</h2>

      <p>An agent can produce a plausible role, amount, and approval story. Prose is not authorization. The policy has to be executable: a denied role stays denied, and a permitted role still carries its MFA / dual-control obligations.</p>

      <p>In this flow, the wrong role gets no transfer, the authorized role gets <code>allow</code> with its obligations attached, and malformed input is rejected by the host contract gate before WASM runs. The path is discover → execute → trace.</p>

      <figure class="post-figure">
        <img src="/assets/img/blog/agent-freestyle-blocked-2026-09-18/demo-host.png" alt="Demo host panel showing traverse-embedder-web driving nested-wasmi runtime.wasm for core.authorize" width="960" height="540" loading="lazy" />
        <figcaption>Host panel: real <code>traverse-embedder-web</code> + nested-wasmi <code>runtime.wasm</code> on the v0.12 path.</figcaption>
      </figure>

      <h2 id="one-runtime">One runtime.wasm. Embedders are clients.</h2>

      <p>The weekly host loads <code>traverse-embedder-web@0.12.0</code>, pins the certified <code>runtime.wasm</code>, and calls <code>core.authorize@1.2.0</code>. The browser, CLI, and MCP are clients of the same orchestrator. The deny belongs to the pinned capability and runtime, not to a demo screen.</p>

      <p>A governed capability evaluates the proposal and denies it.</p>

      <h2 id="what-happened">What happened</h2>

      <div class="verify-table-wrap">
        <table class="verify-table">
          <thead>
            <tr><th>Path</th><th>Result</th></tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td>Cheat — <code>junior_analyst</code> + <code>payments.transfer</code> on a $2.4M wire</td><td><code>deny</code> / <code>no_matching_rule</code></td></tr>
            <tr><td>Legit — <code>treasury_ops</code></td><td><code>allow</code> + MFA / dual-control obligations</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Malformed input</td><td>Host contract gate rejects before WASM</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <h2 id="facts-for-agents">Facts for agents</h2>

      <div class="facts-block" id="agent-facts">
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Theme:</strong> Agent freestyle → blocked (week of 2026-09-18)</li>
          <li><strong>Runnable demo:</strong> <a href="https://github.com/traverse-framework/weekly-demo-2026-09-18-agent-blocked" target="_blank" rel="noopener">github.com/traverse-framework/weekly-demo-2026-09-18-agent-blocked</a></li>
          <li><strong>Capability:</strong> <code>core.authorize@1.2.0</code></li>
          <li><strong>Runtime line:</strong> Traverse <strong>v0.12.0</strong> / <code>traverse-embedder-web@0.12.0</code> via nested-wasmi <code>runtime.wasm</code></li>
          <li><strong>runtime.wasm digest:</strong> <code>sha256:e8d8c04b8927becb5deab9f33da81dd1c121954993ba8b83ea71a2c37cd45e70</code> (certified 0.11.0, unchanged in 0.12.0)</li>
          <li><strong>Cheat outcome:</strong> <code>junior_analyst</code> + <code>payments.transfer</code> / $2.4M → <code>deny</code> / <code>no_matching_rule</code></li>
          <li><strong>Legit outcome:</strong> <code>treasury_ops</code> → <code>allow</code> + MFA / dual-control obligations</li>
          <li><strong>Malformed:</strong> host contract gate rejects before WASM</li>
          <li><strong>Lead claim:</strong> agent proposes, runtime decides · discover → execute → trace</li>
          <li><strong>Packaging caveat:</strong> npm is tagged <code>0.12.0</code>, but <code>releaseEvidence()</code> / <code>PACKAGE_VERSION</code> in the published dist still report <code>0.9.0</code>. The website lockfile also lagged the npm tag; these version surfaces are not yet in lockstep.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <p>A deny that sticks: the agent proposes; the runtime decides.</p>

    </article>

    <aside class="post-sidebar">
      <div class="sidebar-card">
        <div class="sidebar-title">In this post</div>
        <ul class="toc-list">
          <li><a href="#why-it-matters">Why it matters</a></li>
          <li><a href="#one-runtime">One runtime.wasm</a></li>
          <li><a href="#what-happened">What happened</a></li>
          <li><a href="#facts-for-agents">Facts for agents</a></li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="sidebar-card">
        <div class="sidebar-title">Related</div>
        <ul class="related-list">
          <li><a href="/blog/ai-agents-need-contracts.html">AI agents need contracts →</a></li>
          <li><a href="/blog/what-discover-proves.html">What /discover proves →</a></li>
          <li><a href="/blog/traverse-0-11-0-runtime-wasm.html">v0.11.0: one runtime.wasm →</a></li>
          <li><a href="/blog/why-next-help-wanted-is-business-shaped.html">Business-shaped help-wanted →</a></li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="sidebar-card sidebar-cta">
        <div class="sidebar-title">Value loop</div>
        <p>Discover a governed capability → execute known behavior → produce a trace. The agent proposes; the runtime decides.</p>
        <a href="/discover.html" class="btn btn-primary btn-sm" style="width:100%;text-align:center;display:block">Try /discover →</a>
      </div>
    </aside>

  </div>
</div>

<section class="cta-band">
  <div class="container" style="text-align:center">
    <h2 class="t-h2" style="margin-bottom:0.75rem">Agent proposes. Runtime decides.</h2>
    <p class="t-body t-muted" style="margin-bottom:2rem;max-width:480px;margin-left:auto;margin-right:auto">A deny that sticks is enforced by the same <code>runtime.wasm</code> and capability across clients.</p>
    <div style="display:flex;gap:1rem;justify-content:center;flex-wrap:wrap">
      <a href="/agents.html" class="btn btn-primary">For AI agents →</a>
      <a href="https://github.com/traverse-framework/weekly-demo-2026-09-18-agent-blocked" class="btn btn-ghost" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Runnable demo →</a>
      <a href="/blog/ai-agents-need-contracts.html" class="btn btn-ghost">Why contracts →</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
`;
---
<SubpageLayout
  title="The agent freestyled a $2.4M wire. The runtime said no. — Traverse Blog"
  description="Weekly demo: junior_analyst invents a $2.4M payments.transfer and gets deny / no_matching_rule from core.authorize@1.2.0 on real traverse-embedder-web + nested-wasmi runtime.wasm (v0.12)."
  canonical="https://traverse-framework.com/blog/agent-freestyle-blocked.html"
  crumbs={[{ label: 'Home', href: '/' }, { label: 'Blog', href: '/blog.html' }]}
>
  <style is:global slot="head">.post-hero-meta { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.75rem; margin-bottom: 1.25rem; flex-wrap: wrap; }
    .post-date { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.78rem; color: var(--fg-muted); }
    .post-hero h1 { max-width: 760px; margin-bottom: 1.5rem; }
    .post-byline { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 1.5rem; font-family: var(--font-body); font-size: 0.875rem; color: var(--fg-muted); flex-wrap: wrap; }
    .post-byline strong { color: var(--fg); font-weight: 500; }
    .post-layout { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 280px; gap: 4rem; padding: 3.5rem 0 5rem; align-items: start; }
    @media (max-width: 900px) { .post-layout { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 2.5rem; } .post-sidebar { order: -1; } }
    .post-prose { max-width: 680px; font-family: var(--font-body); font-size: 1rem; line-height: 1.75; color: var(--fg); }
    .post-prose p { margin: 0 0 1.4rem; }
    .post-prose h2 { font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: 1.35rem; font-weight: 600; margin: 2.5rem 0 1rem; color: var(--fg); }
    .post-prose ol, .post-prose ul { margin: 0 0 1.4rem 1.25rem; }
    .post-prose li { margin-bottom: 0.5rem; }
    .post-prose a { color: var(--accent); text-decoration: underline; text-decoration-color: var(--accent-dim); }
    .post-prose a:hover { text-decoration-color: var(--accent); }
    .post-prose code { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.85em; background: var(--bg-elevated); padding: 0.15em 0.4em; border-radius: 4px; color: var(--accent); }
    .callout { background: var(--bg-elevated); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-left: 3px solid var(--accent); border-radius: 0 8px 8px 0; padding: 1rem 1.25rem; margin: 1.75rem 0; font-size: 0.92rem; color: var(--fg-muted); line-height: 1.6; }
    .post-figure { margin: 1.75rem 0; }
    .post-figure img { width: 100%; height: auto; border-radius: 10px; border: 1px solid var(--border); background: var(--bg-elevated); }
    .post-figure figcaption { margin-top: 0.65rem; font-size: 0.82rem; color: var(--fg-muted); line-height: 1.5; }
    .verify-table-wrap { overflow-x: auto; margin: 1.75rem 0; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 10px; }
    .verify-table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: 0.875rem; }
    .verify-table th { text-align: left; padding: 0.7rem 1rem; background: var(--bg-elevated); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); font-weight: 600; font-size: 0.72rem; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.05em; color: var(--fg-muted); }
    .verify-table td { padding: 0.7rem 1rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); color: var(--fg-muted); vertical-align: top; }
    .verify-table tr:last-child td { border-bottom: none; }
    .verify-table td:first-child { color: var(--fg); font-weight: 500; }
    .facts-block { background: var(--bg-card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 10px; padding: 1.1rem 1.25rem; margin: 1.25rem 0 1.75rem; }
    .facts-block ul { margin: 0; padding-left: 1.1rem; }
    .facts-block li { margin-bottom: 0.45rem; font-size: 0.9rem; color: var(--fg-muted); line-height: 1.55; }
    .facts-block li strong { color: var(--fg); font-weight: 600; }
    .post-sidebar { position: sticky; top: calc(var(--nav-h) + 2rem); display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 1.5rem; }
    .sidebar-card { background: var(--bg-card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 10px; padding: 1.25rem; }
    .sidebar-title { font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: 0.75rem; font-weight: 600; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.08em; color: var(--fg-muted); margin-bottom: 0.9rem; }
    .toc-list { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.4rem; }
    .toc-list a { font-family: var(--font-body); font-size: 0.83rem; color: var(--fg-muted); text-decoration: none; display: block; padding: 0.2rem 0.6rem; border-left: 2px solid transparent; transition: color 0.15s, border-color 0.15s; }
    .toc-list a:hover { color: var(--fg); border-left-color: var(--accent); }
    .related-list { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.6rem; }
    .related-list a { font-family: var(--font-body); font-size: 0.83rem; color: var(--fg-muted); text-decoration: none; line-height: 1.4; }
    .related-list a:hover { color: var(--accent); }
    .sidebar-cta { background: linear-gradient(135deg, var(--bg-elevated), var(--bg-card)); border-color: var(--accent-dim); }
    .sidebar-cta p { font-family: var(--font-body); font-size: 0.83rem; color: var(--fg-muted); margin: 0 0 1rem; line-height: 1.55; }</style>
  <Fragment set:html={_body} />
</SubpageLayout>
